; Isolates the `@ignore` comment-DSL directive: the open struct-map tolerate-and-drop rest-row
; flavor. Unknown map entries are typed-deserialized (key AND value, so the stream advances) and
; then DROPPED — no `rest` field is generated, and serialize re-emits only the declared members.
; Rejected under --preserve-encodings (a preserve crate's byte-exact contract cannot hold for a
; deliberately lossy type), so this fixture is generation-skipped under the preserve profile
; (registered in snapshot_tests::PROFILE_GENERATION_SKIP and feature_corpus_compiles's
; EXPECTED_GENERATION_FAIL); default/json generate the closed-struct surface.
;
; The `; @ignore` must sit on its own line before the closing `}`: a CDDL comment runs to the end of
; the line, so `; @ignore }` would swallow the brace.
ignored = {
  1: uint,
  * uint => text ; @ignore
}
